{
  "cdmVersionRange": ">=5.0.0",
  "_README": [
    "Lower-extremity wound, ulcer, gangrene, cellulitis, osteomyelitis and diabetic foot, for the Table 1 indication row.",
    "Starts from the target cohort's wound indication (cohort 9100011, 24 roots with descendants) and ADDS five gangrene roots that",
    "cohort lacks (2026-11-05): 4263116 Gangrene (with Dry, Wet, Trophic and Symmetrical gangrene beneath it), 44782426 Gangrene due",
    "to peripheral vascular disease, 35615085 Bilateral gangrene of feet, and the two organism-specific gas gangrene concepts 4141477",
    "and 4142822. Without them generic, dry and wet gangrene codes were not counted as a wound. Non-extremity gangrene (hernia, bowel,",
    "Fournier, upper limb) is deliberately left out.",
    "Limit=All at all three levels with EndStrategy StartDate+0 (same as every other covariate cohort here), so a cohort entry is a single dated event."
  ],
